<task id="012" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rung 0 (explicit-ref / caller-supplied regarding) + Rung 1 (thread continuity) across 8 targets</title>
    <phase>Wave 1 — Server: enrichment + deterministic engine</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>011</dependencies>
    <blocks>015, 030</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Implements deterministic rung logic in the live Association Engine; reimplements retired `EmailAssociationService` thread-continuity design; touches association output for all 8 targets; must preserve engine contract from 011 and respect ADR-024 / ADR-045 + bff-extensions governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-rungs</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement the two deterministic rungs on top of the Association Engine (task 011), each as an `IAssociationRung`, operating over the `NormalizedMessage` envelope, emitting per-attribute confidence + provenance, across all eight targets (matter, project, invoice, service request, work assignment, event, contact, organization):

    • **Rung 0 — explicit reference / caller-supplied regarding.** A caller-supplied regarding (e.g. from the outbound send request or add-in save pane) is treated as rung 0 (highest determinism). Also extend the subject-line explicit-reference regex (matter/invoice/service-request identifiers) to resolve explicit tokens in the subject.

    • **Rung 1 — thread continuity.** Using `inReplyTo` / `references[]` / `conversationId` from the envelope, find the parent `sprk_communication` and COPY its regarding to the new communication. Reimplement the `conversationindex` correlation logic from the RETIRED `EmailAssociationService` design (signal design only — reuse the algorithm, not the deleted code; the OOB-email subsystem is retired in W0 task 007).

    Both rungs run for inbound AND outbound (direction symmetry). Do NOT implement rung 2/3 (tasks 013/014) or the confidence→status ladder (task 015) — emit `RungMatch` results with confidence + provenance; task 015 maps them to status.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer, Association Engine rung author. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-024 (regarding family — write typed lookups + denormalized fields), the engine/rung contract from task 011, ADR-045, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Rung 0 (explicit-ref + caller-supplied regarding) and Rung 1 (thread continuity via `inReplyTo`/`references`/`conversationId` → parent comm → copy regarding, reimplementing `conversationindex` logic) are implemented as ordered `IAssociationRung`s, resolving across all 8 targets, emitting confidence + provenance, running symmetrically for inbound + outbound. Build clean; per-rung + direction-symmetry tests pass (authored here or referenced from 017); publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 011 delivered the Association Engine over the normalized envelope with an `IAssociationRung` abstraction and a `RungMatch` (target ref + per-attribute confidence + provenance). Tasks 012–014 fill in the deterministic rung content. Task 012 owns the two highest-determinism rungs.

      Rung 0 has two sources: (a) an explicit caller-supplied regarding (outbound send request, add-in save pane), which is authoritative, and (b) explicit identifiers in the subject line (extend the existing subject regex). Rung 1 is thread continuity: mail threading headers (`inReplyTo`, `references`) plus Graph `conversationId` let us find the parent `sprk_communication` and inherit its regarding — this is the single highest-value deterministic signal for ongoing matters. The `conversationindex` correlation algorithm from the now-retired `EmailAssociationService` (deleted in W0 task 007) is reused as DESIGN only; reimplement it against the envelope.

      Eight targets: matter, project, invoice, service request, work assignment, event, contact, organization — resolved through the ADR-024 regarding machinery (catalog/map/priority extended in W0 tasks 003/004).
    </background>
