  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read the task-011 engine contract note + `IAssociationRung`/`RungMatch` to confirm the rung signature and provenance shape.</step>
    <step order="2">Read the W0 catalog/map/priority extensions (service request, event, organization targets) so rung matches resolve all 8 targets through the ADR-024 machinery.</step>
    <step order="3">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + ADR-024 before writing rung output.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement Rung 0: (a) accept a caller-supplied regarding (from the send request / add-in context) as an authoritative rung-0 match; (b) extend the subject explicit-reference regex to detect matter/invoice/service-request identifiers; emit `RungMatch` with high deterministic confidence + provenance citing the source (caller vs subject-token).</step>
    <step order="5">Implement Rung 1 (thread continuity): from the envelope's `inReplyTo`/`references[]`/`conversationId`, query for the parent `sprk_communication`; if found, copy its regarding to the new communication. Reimplement the `conversationindex` correlation algorithm from the retired `EmailAssociationService` design. Emit `RungMatch` + provenance citing the parent comm id and the matched header(s).</step>
    <step order="6">Register both rungs in `CommunicationModule` in the correct order (rung 0 before rung 1); confirm the Engine iterates them ahead of rungs 2/3.</step>
    <step order="7">Write per-rung unit tests + direction-symmetry tests (inbound and outbound produce identical rung-0/rung-1 matches for equivalent envelopes) in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`. Coordinate scope with task 017 (which owns the cross-rung symmetry suite) to avoid duplication.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm the task-011 characterization tests still pass (no regression).</step>
    <step order="8.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/r4-012-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="8.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-10 rungs 0–1 + ADR-024 + direction symmetry). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; note 013/014 are parallel siblings — confirm no overlapping edits to shared engine files).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (012 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (subject-regex extensions, `conversationindex` reimplementation choices).</step>
  </steps>

